negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 36     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  First is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm breast with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm skin ellipse containing a 4 5cm curvilinear scar located 3 0cm below the nipple  Underneath the scar  there is an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  red area with eccentric cavitation  located 1 0cm from the inferior margin and 4 0cm from the deep margin  Surrounding this area  is an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm ill defined area of parenchyma which stands out from the surrounding tissue  This area is composed of more solid  firm stellate regions  with intervening firm  gritty fibrous bands with interspersed yellow fat lobules  and studded with numerous punctate yellow  soft  and hard foci  This region extends within 0 5cm of the inferior margin  0 1cm of the medial margin  and 1 5cm of the deep margin medially  The remaining breast parenchyma has a fine  pink nodular texture in the fibrous bands with unremarkable intervening fatty tissue  focally  yellow punctate foci are also noted  Scattered cysts are present  and the parenchyma closer to skin has a dense white texture  Unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 2 0cm are present in the axillary fat  Section code  A  inferior margin B C  medial margin D  deep margin E G  other sections of firm area H  red biopsy site I J  tissue adjacent to the tumor  I includes inferior margin K  sections of remaining parenchyma including dense white areas  finely pink nodular areas  and punctate yellow foci L R  axillary lymph nodes Labeled  axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty aggregate containing a small 0 3cm lymph node  one half in cassette S  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION , Mastectomy.
